## 1. Company Profile

### Main business

Tencent Music Entertainment Group (TME) is China's largest online music platform operator. It owns three core products: QQ Music, Kugou Music, and Kuwo Music, as well as social entertainment applications such as National Karaoke. The company belongs to the Tencent Holdings ecosystem and is the absolute leader in China's online music market.

### Revenue structure (full year 2025)

| Business Segment | Revenue (100 million yuan) | Proportion | Year-on-year growth rate |
|---------|------------|------|---------|
| Online music subscriptions | 176.6 | 53.7% | +16.0% |
| Online music non-subscription (advertising, concerts, etc.) | 90.7 | 27.6% | +39.2% |
| Social Entertainment | 61.8 | 18.8% | -7.3% |
| **Total** | **329.0** | **100%** | **+15.8%** |

### Market position

- China's online music market share is approximately 69%, far exceeding NetEase Cloud Music (approximately 19%) and Soda Music
- The number of online music paying users reached 127.4 million (by the end of 2025), a year-on-year increase of 5.3%
- The number of super member (SVIP) users exceeded 20 million
- Average monthly revenue per paying user (ARPPU) increased by 7.2% year-on-year to 11.9 yuan

